WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:01.038
Who's this for?

2
00:00:01.038 --> 00:00:05.697
The developers and platform engineers who
write server baselines for the Arc track,

3
00:00:05.697 --> 00:00:08.825
and the engineers and security
officers who review them.

4
00:00:08.825 --> 00:00:12.846
You'll want to be comfortable in
PowerShell and know what a desired state

5
00:00:12.846 --> 00:00:16.800
configuration is; the chapter covers
the parts of Azure Policy you need.

6
00:00:16.800 --> 00:00:18.762
The roles are few and narrow.

7
00:00:18.762 --> 00:00:22.324
Publishing a definition needs
the policy contributor role.

8
00:00:22.324 --> 00:00:25.592
Machines read the package
with their own identity

9
00:00:25.592 --> 00:00:28.237
and a read-only storage
role, never a token.

10
00:00:28.237 --> 00:00:32.400
And the remediation role is the one
to confirm before you rely on it.
